; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Dice Histogram
; CATEGORY: Lists & Data Structures
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     arrays, counting, random, bar chart, tally
; SUMMARY:  Rolls two dice hundreds of times, tallies each total in an array and draws the results as a growing bar chart.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   When you roll two dice, totals from 2 to 12 are possible, but
;   they are not equally likely. The program keeps one counter for
;   each total in an array whose first index is 2, rolls the dice
;   500 times, and redraws the chart every 50 rolls so you can watch
;   the famous hill shape appear, highest at 7.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch the bars grow. Change ROLLS for more rolls.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * an ARRAY used as a row of tally counters
;   * starting an array at index 2 with (ARRAY 11 2)
;   * ITEM and SETITEM to add one to a counter
;   * scaling bars so the chart always fits
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Roll three dice. How many counters do you need now?
;   * Print which total came up most often.
;   * Compare with one die rolled twice as often.
; ============================================================

make "rolls 500

; (ARRAY 11 2) makes 11 slots numbered 2 to 12, one for each total,
; so the total itself can be used as the index.
make "tally (array 11 2)
for [t 2 12] [setitem :t :tally 0]

to roll
  output (1 + random 6) + (1 + random 6)
end

to bump :total
  setitem :total :tally 1 + item :total :tally
end

; The tallest bar is scaled to 380 steps, so the chart always fits.
to drawchart :done
  clean
  localmake "biggest reduce [ifelse ?1 > ?2 [?1] [?2]] arraytolist :tally
  if :biggest = 0 [make "biggest 1]
  for [t 2 12] [
    localmake "h 380 * (item :t :tally) / :biggest
    localmake "x -330 + 60 * (:t - 2)
    penup setxy :x -220 setheading 90
    setpencolor ifelse :t = 7 ["red] ["blue]
    pendown filled pencolor [repeat 2 [fd 44 lt 90 fd :h lt 90]]
    penup setxy :x + 12 -245 setpencolor "black label :t
    setxy :x + 8 -212 + :h label item :t :tally
  ]
  penup setxy -330 230
  label (sentence [Two dice, rolled] :done [times])
end

clearscreen hideturtle
repeat :rolls / 50 [
  repeat 50 [bump roll]
  drawchart 50 * repcount
  wait 20
]
print sentence [Final tallies from 2 to 12:] arraytolist :tally
